{
  "company_name": "StockSmart Distribution",
  "industry": "Industrial Distribution",
  "use_case": "Warehouse inventory optimization and stock level management",
  "space_title": "StockSmart Distribution - Inventory Optimization 📦",
  "space_description": "**Scenario:** You manage inventory across StockSmart Distribution's three DCs in Chicago, Houston, and Atlanta, holding 20 warehouse-product combos spanning pipe fittings, power tools, abrasives, cutting tools, and welding consumables. Your CFO wants turns up toward the 6-8 best-in-class mark, but cash is trapped in slow-moving overstock in one DC while another keeps stocking out and losing the sale. Where is your inventory misallocated across the network, and which items should you rebalance first?\n\n**Questions:**\n\n1. Showcase the different visualization options with interesting aspects of the dataset (agent)\n2. What is my current inventory position by warehouse, product category, and stock status? (agent)\n3. Which warehouses have the highest carrying cost paired with the lowest turnover ratio, and which warehouse-product combos sit below reorder point? (agent)",
  "schema_basename": "distro_inventory_opt",
