  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Warehouse Inventory Optimization for an industrial distributor running 3 distribution centers (Chicago, Houston, Atlanta) holding 20 warehouse-product combinations across pipe fittings, power tools, abrasives, cutting tools, and welding consumables. Stakeholders include the Supply Planner (reorder points, days-of-supply), Branch Manager (stockouts, fill rate), Category Manager (turnover, slow-moving SKUs), and CFO (carrying cost, inventory investment).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Inventory turnover = avg_turnover_ratio (inventory_snapshots); industrial distribution benchmark 4-6 turns/year, best-in-class 6-8\n- Days of supply / DOH = avg_days_of_supply; flag >120 days as slow-moving\n- Fill rate = avg_fill_rate (fill_rate_pct on inventory_snapshots); MRO target ≥97%\n- Stockout count / days = stockout_count (snapshots in Stockout status) and total_stockout_days\n- Carrying cost = total_carrying_cost (weekly) and total_monthly_carrying_cost; typically 20-30% of inventory value/yr\n- Inventory value = on_hand_qty * unit_cost_usd (use the `inventory value USD` snippet)\n- Below reorder = on_hand_qty < reorder_point (use the `below reorder point` snippet)\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - inventory_kpi_monthly (source: inventory_transactions) — dims: snapshot_date, warehouse, product_category, stock_status; measures: avg_on_hand_qty, total_carrying_cost, avg_days_of_supply, stockout_count, total_snapshot_count, unique_wp_count, max_on_hand_qty, total_reorder_point.\n  - inventory_perf_monthly (source: inventory_snapshots) — dims: perf_month, warehouse, product_category; measures: avg_turnover_ratio, total_stockout_days, avg_fill_rate, total_monthly_carrying_cost, item_count, max_turnover_ratio.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. wp_id, product_name, unit_cost_usd, reorder_point, optimization_action).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Showcase the different visualization options with interesting aspects of the dataset",
    "What is my current inventory position by warehouse, product category, and stock status?",
    "Which warehouses have the highest carrying cost paired with the lowest turnover ratio, and which warehouse-product combos sit below reorder point?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "How many distinct snapshots appeared each month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', snapshot_date) AS month, COUNT(DISTINCT snapshot) AS distinct_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.inventory_transactions",
        "GROUP BY 1",
        "ORDER BY 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has highest on hand qty changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, MEASURE(max_on_hand_qty) AS max_on_hand_qty",
        "FROM {fqn}.inventory_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has average number of stockout days in month trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT perf_month, AVG(stockout_days) AS avg_stockout_days",
        "FROM {fqn}.inventory_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY perf_month",
        "ORDER BY perf_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total monthly carrying cost changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT perf_month, MEASURE(total_monthly_carrying_cost) AS total_monthly_carrying_cost",
        "FROM {fqn}.inventory_perf_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY perf_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does units moved compare across products?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT product_name, SUM(quantity_moved) AS total_quantity_moved",
        "FROM {fqn}.warehouse_products",
        "GROUP BY product_name",
        "ORDER BY product_name",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total units on hand over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(on_hand_qty) AS total_on_hand_qty",
        "FROM {fqn}.inventory_transactions",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average inventory turnover ratio changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT perf_month, AVG(turnover_ratio) AS avg_turnover_ratio",
        "FROM {fqn}.inventory_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY perf_month ORDER BY perf_month"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sql_snippets": {
    "filters": [
      {
        "sql": "inventory_transactions.stock_status = 'Stockout'",
        "display_name": "stockouts",
        "synonyms": [
          "out of stock"
        ],
        "instruction": "Filter to stockout items."
      },
      {
        "sql": "inventory_transactions.stock_status = 'Overstock'",
        "display_name": "overstocked",
        "synonyms": [
          "excess inventory"
        ],
        "instruction": "Filter to overstocked items."
      },
      {
        "sql": "warehouse_products.movement_type = 'Issue'",
        "display_name": "issues",
        "synonyms": [
          "outbound",
          "shipments"
        ],
        "instruction": "Filter to inventory issues."
      }
    ],
    "expressions": [
      {
        "alias": "movement_month",
        "sql": "DATE_TRUNC('month', warehouse_products.movement_date)",
        "display_name": "movement month",
        "synonyms": [
          "monthly"
        ]
      },
      {
        "alias": "inventory_value",
        "sql": "inventory_transactions.on_hand_qty * warehouse_products.unit_cost_usd",
        "display_name": "inventory value USD",
        "synonyms": [
          "stock value"
        ]
      },
      {
        "alias": "below_reorder",
        "sql": "CASE WHEN inventory_transactions.on_hand_qty < inventory_transactions.reorder_point THEN 'Yes' ELSE 'No' END",
        "display_name": "below reorder point",
        "synonyms": [
          "needs reorder"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "measures": [
      {
        "alias": "avg_on_hand",
        "sql": "AVG(inventory_transactions.on_hand_qty)",
        "display_name": "average on-hand qty",
        "synonyms": [
          "stock level"
        ]
      },
      {
        "alias": "total_carrying_cost",
        "sql": "SUM(inventory_transactions.carrying_cost_usd)",
        "display_name": "total carrying cost",
        "synonyms": [
          "holding cost"
        ]
      },
      {
        "alias": "avg_turnover",
        "sql": "AVG(inventory_snapshots.turnover_ratio)",
        "display_name": "average turnover",
        "synonyms": [
          "turns"
        ]
      },
      {
        "alias": "avg_fill_rate",
        "sql": "AVG(inventory_snapshots.fill_rate_pct)",
        "display_name": "average fill rate",
        "synonyms": [
          "service level"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
